## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the two; any removed or changed line; any byte under `src`, `docs`, `web`, `.github`, a project file; a skip, `.only`-style gate, environment gate or sleep in an added row; a lost test name; a non-ASCII byte, ticket key, finding or mutant id, percent figure or person's name in an added line or message; a secret; **a build warning, a failed or skipped test on the merge ref, or any PR check-run failed or cancelled**; a new open alert; the head moved; the Fail half of the new rows NOT red at base `a5b4bbb5` (or red for another reason); the calculator's `ContractSuppliesCost` not the exact figure. *Major:* **B567-5 not closed: any "round the recomputed side" variant (any `MidpointRounding`) that survives, or is killed only by a pre-existing row**; B567-6 not closed (M12 survives); a non-equivalent survivor you cannot prove equivalent; a new row that no mutant turns red and is not a declared control; a planted reported figure on a midpoint or a fixture property not met; a differential disagreement (or no power under the control mutants); a builder claim contradicted (15 names, 13 ran / 4 red at base, Engine 427 then 428, Import 167, Api 2204, 8 of 8 killed); a repeat red. *Minor/Note:* M11 survives (ruled); the builder's fixture differing from the brief's suggestion (if your figures confirm the original hit a midpoint); the pre-existing killers of the rounded-reported/difference mutants (the brief's wording was wrong for those, the builder said so); the header-comment nit; the round-1 Notes not built; CI timing; the timing-sensitive Api test passing on rerun.
**ROUND-CAP STATEMENT (binding; copy it into your STATUS verdict section).** This is **round 2 of 2, the cap.** For EVERY finding say whether it is a closed instance of the round-1 class (B567-5, B567-6) or a new one. A GO or GO WITH FINDINGS lets Tuesday land #106 once the checks are green. **A NO GO does not start a round 3: the closed instances stay closed (nothing is reverted; the PR keeps what you proved), the rest is ticketed, and a third round needs the product owner's word** (Tuesday writes the card). Do not soften a Major to avoid that; do not harden a Minor to force it.

**First line of STATUS:** `GATE VERDICT B576: #106 b565 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 4ef1adc (round 2 of 2 - THE CAP - delta <2 commits, 2 paths, +165 -0 y/n; src/docs/web/.github bytes 0 y/n; existing lines untouched y/n; names lost n added n> - fixture <ContractSuppliesCost exact at 12 and 24 y/n; remainders opposite y/n; midpoints hit 0 y/n> - red-first <13 ran, 4 red at base for the right reason y/n; 14 of 14 and 427 then 428 y/n> - mutants <killed n of m; round-recomputed-side variants killed by new rows only y/n; survivors <names|none>; M12 killed y/n; M11 survives as ruled y/n; controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n> - differential <seed 576101, n checks, disagreements n, power n> - CI line on the merge ref <Engine n, Import n, Api n, warnings n, failed n> - checks <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <open alerts n, analyses n of 4> - merge <mergeable, mergeable_state, 2 ahead 0 behind y/n> - lanes sharing a path <n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict, incl. the merge ref and its parents), instrument and load, your predictions (written first), checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B576-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, closed-instance or new, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the mutant table and the row-kill table, the check-run table with the PENDING set per poll, the ROUND-CAP STATEMENT, FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether #106 can land now; "the PR #106 checks are <state>"), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports, slots and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B576 #106 b565/mps-readiness-reconciliation-hardening @ 4ef1adc <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 2 of 2, the cap; PR #106 open; CI <complete|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (m